<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="chapter-context" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>The Context for Statistics</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      The course starts with three outcomes focus on the context of
      statistic. Where is statistics used? What is the situation and
      setup where statistics is valuable? What are the choice made in
      setting up a formal study? What are the moral and ethoical
      dimensions of such a formal study? 
    </p>
    <p>
      I want to start with context to situation the rest of the
      course. I doesn't make sense to talk about the formal technique
      of statistics without having a clear sense of where the
      technique is used and the basic paramater that govern is
      appropriate and ethically reasonable use. 
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="clo1-vocabulary.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="clo2-study-design.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="clo3-study-ethics.ptx" />

</chapter>
